    "threads": [
      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on scope and pick which vehicles join the initial pilot",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, kicking off the new Fleet Maintenance and Workshop Safety Standardization project. The goal is to make our routines consistent and safer. First step is T10: we need to pilot the new procedures. Any thoughts on which vehicles we should start with?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "truck",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Maybe the oldest trucks? The ones that always seem to have problems. We could see if the new checks catch things earlier.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "That's one approach, but if we only use the oldest vehicles, our feedback might be skewed towards wear-and-tear issues. To get a balanced view, we should probably test on a mix of vehicle types and ages. For example, a couple of the high-usage front-loaders and a couple of the older side-loaders.",
            "mentions": [
              38857
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 156061,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "I agree with a mix. How about two of the newer Volvo front-loaders that do the city routes and two of the older Dennis Eagle side-loaders for the residential collections? That covers different usage patterns.",
            "mentions": [
              109283
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "So four trucks in total for the pilot?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "The task T10 just says a 'small subset'. Let's make it five to get a slightly better sample. How about we add one of the smaller Isuzu trucks that handles the tight access lanes? So, 2 Volvos, 2 Dennis Eagles, and 1 Isuzu.",
            "mentions": [
              156061
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "That's a solid mix. It covers our main workhorses without causing too much disruption. We should also make sure the weekly deep-check routine from T2 is applied to the Volvos in that group, since they have the highest mileage.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Good point. Okay, so we're set on the vehicles. What about duration? I suggest we run the pilot for one full week. That should be enough time to see if the new process flows well or causes delays.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "When would we start?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "We can't start until the first draft of the daily checklist is ready. I suggest we aim to start the pilot next Monday. That gives us this week to prepare the initial documents.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "calendar",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "Perfect. Let's lock that in. I'll summarize the decisions here.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Decision: The pilot will include five vehicles: two Volvo front-loaders, two Dennis Eagle side-loaders, and one Isuzu truck.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
