      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Draft and finalise the daily inspection checklist and weekly routine",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Morning all. As per T1, I've put together a first draft of the 'Daily Vehicle Inspection Checklist' (A1). It's in the shared folder, please take a look and give me your feedback.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "page_facing_up",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "I had a look. It seems a bit long for a daily check. Do we really need to check hydraulic fluid levels every single day before roll-out?",
            "mentions": [
              108987
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Yeah, that takes a few minutes per truck. We usually do that as part of the weekly checks.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "That's a valid point. The daily check should be a quick safety and roadworthiness inspection - tyres, lights, horn, mirrors, visual leak check. Things that can be done in 5 minutes. Deeper mechanical checks like fluid levels, brake pad wear, and filter inspections belong in the weekly deep-check routine we're defining in T2.",
            "mentions": [
              203126,
              38857
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 156061,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Exactly. We should stick to the 'no tools' rule for daily checks. If you need to open a toolbox, it's not a daily check. This is part of mapping our current steps for T7 to cut out redundant actions. Let's keep the daily list focused on what prevents roadside breakdowns and safety issues.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "Great feedback, everyone. That makes perfect sense. I'll update the 'Daily Vehicle Inspection Checklist' (A1) right now to only include the quick, no-tool visual checks. I'll move the other items to a separate draft for the T2 weekly routine.",
            "mentions": [
              109283,
              156061
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "rocket",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Okay, the updated A1 is in the folder. It's much shorter now. The weekly checks are in a new doc. Can we agree on this structure?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "This looks much more practical for daily use. I approve this structure. Let's formalize it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "Decision: The daily inspection checklist (A1) is approved with a focus on visual, no-tool checks for safety and roadworthiness.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
