      {
        "thread_id": "TH5",
        "thread_goal": "Plan training, shift handovers and weekly review cadence",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M74",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, let's sort out the final pieces of this project: handovers (T6), new staff training (T8), and our weekly reviews (T12). How do we want to manage these?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6",
              "T8",
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M75",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M74",
            "text": "For handovers, we normally just leave a few notes on the whiteboard for the next shift.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M76",
            "speaker_id": 156061,
            "reply_to": "M75",
            "text": "That's not very reliable. Whiteboard notes can get erased by accident. We need a proper 'Shift Handover Notes Template' (A5) as described in T6. It should be a digital file with clear sections: 'Open Issues', 'Parts on Order', and 'Priorities for Next Shift'. That way there's a permanent record.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M77",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M76",
            "text": "A digital log is the right way to go. It's auditable and nothing gets lost. We should make it mandatory to fill it out in the last 15 minutes of every shift.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M78",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M77",
            "text": "I agree. I can create the A5 template in a shared doc. Let's make that official.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M79",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M78",
            "text": "Decision: We will use a standard digital 'Shift Handover Notes Template' (A5), which must be completed at the end of each shift.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D9"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M80",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M79",
            "text": "What about training for new people? Do they have to read all these new documents?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M81",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M80",
            "text": "The documents are for reference. For T8, we need a simple 'New Staff Maintenance and Safety Training Brief' (A7). It should be a short, two-page summary of the critical items: how to use the daily checklist, where the incident log is, and what the 'DO NOT USE' tag means. We should also pair them with an experienced attendant for their first week.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8",
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M82",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M81",
            "text": "That's a good plan. I can draft that brief (A7). Lastly, the weekly review from T12. We need a set time to review the incident log and the pilot feedback summary (A8) to see what we can improve. I propose every Friday at 2 PM, during the shift changeover.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7",
              "T12",
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M83",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M82",
            "text": "Who needs to be at that meeting?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M84",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M83",
            "text": "To be effective, we need at least one person from each shift to attend, so all perspectives are heard. The fleet supervisor should be invited as well.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M85",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M84",
            "text": "Okay, let's lock that in. I'll book a recurring meeting for us.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M86",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M85",
            "text": "Decision: A weekly review meeting will be held every Friday at 2 PM. Attendance is mandatory for at least one attendant from each shift.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D10"
